00:37:52.650 --> 00:37:57.309
[S12] going to get, you know, I don't know, Larry Page's principles or X, Y, Z's principles

581
00:37:57.309 --> 00:37:58.730
[S12] for that situation.

582
00:37:58.730 --> 00:38:03.289
[S12] And you have that there, and then you have your own principles, and you write it down.

583
00:38:03.289 --> 00:38:07.309
[S12] So that when you're then in a situation, you could look at that situation, and you

584
00:38:07.309 --> 00:38:10.900
[S12] say, what should I do going to those principles?

585
00:38:10.900 --> 00:38:15.170
[S12] So, because if you start to think of that in the principled way, it's, it's very helpful,

586
00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:16.230
[S12] and they will refine.

587
00:38:16.230 --> 00:38:17.230
[S13] Gotcha.

588
00:38:17.230 --> 00:38:23.119
[S13] Now, in the five-step process, what's the, of the five steps, what do people have the

589
00:38:23.119 --> 00:38:24.480
[S13] most trouble with?

590
00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:26.199
[S12] It's very interesting.

591
00:38:26.199 --> 00:38:30.650
[S12] It really depends on how their brains work.

592
00:38:30.650 --> 00:38:38.309
[S12] Like, there are some real big-picture thinkers who, you know, have no problems with goals.

593
00:38:38.309 --> 00:38:44.869
[S12] They know where they want to go, but they have problems pushing through to results.

594
00:38:44.869 --> 00:38:52.369
[S12] So, there are some people in terms of diagnosing things to the root cause, it's a challenge.

595
00:38:52.369 --> 00:38:55.980
[S12] Everybody has a problem at one of those steps.

596
00:38:55.980 --> 00:39:02.809
[S12] And we see that by observing themselves as to which step they have a problem with, they

597
00:39:02.809 --> 00:39:06.170
[S12] begin to understand how their brain works.

598
00:39:06.170 --> 00:39:10.039
[S12] It's not a problem, though, if they work collectively.

599
00:39:10.039 --> 00:39:15.119
[S12] Because whatever step they're having a problem with, another person, if they help them with

600
00:39:15.119 --> 00:39:18.309
[S12] that, can really help them be effective at that step.

601
00:39:18.309 --> 00:39:21.369
[S12] And that's really the key to success in life.

602
00:39:21.369 --> 00:39:26.340
[S12] The key to success in life, really, is largely knowing what you're not good at, and who

603
00:39:26.340 --> 00:39:32.500
[S12] can help you be good at those things, so that you can lean on each other and be effective.

604
00:39:32.500 --> 00:39:33.500
[S13] Excellent.

