00:39:56.269 --> 00:40:03.170
[S12] late stage, the stage I'm now at, he described returning the boon.

610
00:40:03.170 --> 00:40:06.190
[S12] And returning the boon is the...

611
00:40:06.610 --> 00:40:11.239
[S14] Stage where, you know, you learned a lot.

612
00:40:11.239 --> 00:40:15.329
[S14] And some people learn a lot and then they go to retirement.

613
00:40:15.329 --> 00:40:23.070
[S14] And he was making the point that when you learn a lot, you pass along that to others.

614
00:40:23.070 --> 00:40:25.820
[S14] And he described it very vividly.

615
00:40:25.820 --> 00:40:30.329
[S14] Like, I don't like public attention.

616
00:40:30.329 --> 00:40:33.300
[S14] I don't like all of that.

617
00:40:33.300 --> 00:40:40.110
[S14] But he described it as, you know, at that last stage, how important it is to pass along

618
00:40:40.110 --> 00:40:41.110
[S14] what you learn.

619
00:40:41.110 --> 00:40:43.210
[S14] He described it as a difficult process.

